str subclass's instance's) value."] [62 1 "// kindFor is the kind of a str whose largest code point is mx, and whether it is ASCII."] [75 1 "// unicodeLayout is the layout of o's mirror: its kind, ASCII flag, compactness (an exact str), length, the data's"] [76 1 "// offset and the bytes it needs."] [105 1 "// storeUnit and loadUnit write and read the character i of a kind k buffer at p."] [129 1 "// writeUnicode writes a str's PyASCIIObject (and its compact or legacy part) and characters at a (the handle's"] [130 1 "// memory, zeroed); a str PyUnicode_New made keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes."] [135 36 "// hash: -1, not computed"] [158 1 "// syncStrFromC copies the characters C wrote into a new str's mirror to the pyi str."] [178 1 "// strMirror is the mirror of a str's handle (nil: not a str), synchronized from C."] [190 1 "// maxCharOf is PyUnicode_MAX_CHAR_VALUE of a str's mirror."] [203 1 "// kindName is unicode_kind_name."] [216 1 "// modifiable is unicode_check_modifiable: a str PyUnicode_New made that C alone holds, not hashed by Python."] [224 1 "// newUnicode is PyUnicode_New(size, maxchar): a str of size NUL characters whose mirror has maxchar's kind, a new"] [225 1 "// reference."] [250 1 "// fromUnits is _PyUnicode_FromUCS1/2/4: the str of n characters of kind k at p (its largest character checked as"] [251 1 "// PyUnicode_New checks it)."] [264 1 "// uwriter is a PyUnicodeWriter: the characters written so far (its C pointer a block of the world's own, so that a"] [265 1 "// cast to _PyUnicodeWriter names the same writer)."] [272 1 "// writeRunes appends a str's characters (or a part of them) to a writer."] [279 1 "// unicodeTable: the natives of the compact layout and of the writer (queue 270)."] [283 2 "// the functions behind the macros (Include/cpython/unicodeobject.h declares them too)"] [296 2 "// PyUnicode_Fill (Objects/unicodeobject.c)"] [323 2 "// PyUnicode_CopyCharacters and _copy_characters (check_maxchar)"] [372 2 "// as_